==Strategy==
This stage is not playing around, as it spams Gobbles like they're peons.

[[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necro-Dancer Cat]] with his [[Immune to Toxic|Toxic Immune]] [[Talents|Talent]], trivializes this stage as long as he's also at a decent level, but without it, a high leveled [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] must be used.

[[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]] with his toxic immune talent is also an excellent choice here.

Fishman should be able to knockback a Gobble in one hit, but in order to do so they must be level 58, level 50 with Attack Buff Talent level 8, or level 50 with Attack Buff Talent level 2 and an Attack Up (Sm) Combo. Cameraman should be able to knockback a Gobble in six hits, but in order to do so they must be level 58, level 50 with Attack Buff Talent level 7, or level 50 with Attack Buff Talent level 2 and a Attack Up (Sm) Combo and should have the [[Survive]] Talent maxed out.

If they are high leveled enough, then its just blindly spamming Cameraman (with Research Combos) to win. Otherwise, you'll need additional support from a well-timed [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] hit, [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]], or other heavy attackers. Rich Cat is highly recommended if your Cameraman is not high leveled enough.

If you have unlocked Awakened Bahamut Cat's Talents, the stage becomes much easier, as you can time 2 Fishman Cats and then use Bahamut to ensure that the Gobbles and Hackey do not hit you (with the help of some Cat Combos.)

